course: dictionary
lesson: 11064
title: A word from another language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Not every word you meet in English is an English word. «Wei» comes from Mandarin Chinese, and it is written in pinyin, the spelling system that uses our letters to show Chinese sounds.
explain: When people in China answer the phone, they often say «wei?», which is like saying «hello?» in English. Context helps you spot this. «Wei says no, politely.» Here Wei starts with a capital letter and does something a person does, so it is a name.
explain: Look for clues around the word. A capital letter and a sentence about what someone does tell you Wei is a person. A phone ringing tells you «wei» is a greeting. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: «Wei» is not an English word. In English texts it is usually a person's name.
fact: In Chinese, «wei» (喂) is what people say when they answer the phone, like «hello?».
fact: Wei is also a common Chinese surname and a given name, and it is the name of some old Chinese kingdoms.
fact: Many Chinese words sound the same, so the tone marks and the context show which one is meant: «wèi» (为) means «for», «wèi» (位) is a polite counting word for people, and «wèi» (胃) means «stomach».
fact: When you meet a word from another language, ask: is this a name, a greeting, or a word I need to look up?
exercise: «Wei says no, politely.» In this sentence, what is Wei most likely to be? | *A person's name | A phone greeting | A polite counting word | A kind of food
exercise: In Chinese, what do people often say when they answer the phone? | Goodbye | Look out | Thank you | *Wei, which is like hello?
exercise: In Chinese, the word «wèi» (胃) means what? | For | Kingdom | *Stomach | A polite counting word
test: Is «wei» an English word? | Yes, it means hello | No, it is a name only in English | *No, it is a Chinese word written in pinyin | Yes, it means stomach
test: Which of these is the name of an old Chinese kingdom? | *Wei | For | Hello | Stomach
exam: Mia hears someone answer the phone with «wei?» in Beijing. What does it most likely mean? | Stomach | Thank you | *Hello? | Goodbye
